React Compiler is enabled in this codebase and automatically memoizes derived values. `tagItems` is a plain derived computation over `searchResults` and `translate` with no refs or effects, so wrapping it in `useMemo` is redundant and interferes with the compiler's own caching. (Please confirm with `check-compiler.sh src/components/Search/FilterComponents/TagSelector.tsx` — if the file fails to compile, this rule does not apply.)

Remove the `useMemo` and compute the value inline so the compiler can memoize it:

```tsx
const tagItems = (() => {
    const items = [{text: translate('search.noTag'), value: CONST.SEARCH.TAG_EMPTY_VALUE as string}];
    const seenTagNames = new Set<string>();
    for (const policyTags of Object.values(searchResults ?? {})) {
        for (const tag of Object.values(policyTags ?? {})) {
            if (seenTagNames.has(tag.tagName)) {
                continue;
            }
            seenTagNames.add(tag.tagName);
            items.push({text: getCleanedTagName(tag.tagName), value: tag.tagName});
        }
    }
    return items;
})();
```

React Compiler is enabled in this codebase and automatically memoizes components, so manual `React.memo` wrappers are normally redundant and interfere with the compiler's own caching model. Here `SearchAdvancedFiltersContent` is wrapped in `React.memo` to skip re-rendering the backgrounded (kept-mounted) filter contents.

The inline comment argues the compiler caches the whole `mountedFilters.map()` result in a single slot and therefore can't bail out per element. Please verify this against the compiler first (`check-compiler.sh` on this file) — if the file compiles, prefer restructuring so the compiler can memoize each element (e.g. extracting the per-filter body, including its wrapper `View`, into its own component rendered inside the `.map()`, so each instance gets independent memoization) rather than hand-wrapping with `React.memo`:

```tsx
function MountedFilterContent({filterKey, isRested, values, onChange}: MountedFilterContentProps) {
    const styles = useThemeStyles();
    return (
        <View style={[styles.flex1, !isRested && [styles.pAbsolute, styles.w100, styles.h100, styles.visibilityHidden]]}>
            <SearchAdvancedFiltersContent values={values} baseFilterKey={filterKey} components={filterComponents} onChange={onChange} />
        </View>
    );
}
```

