React Compiler is enabled in this codebase and automatically memoizes derived values inside components. Wrapping `sortedCategoryItems` in a manual `useMemo` is redundant here — the computation is a plain pure derivation (sort + `moveInitialSelectionToTop`) from `categoryItems`, `initialSelectedCategories`, and `localeCompare`, which is exactly what the compiler caches on its own. The manual wrapper adds a dependency array that must be maintained and can interfere with the compiler's own caching.

Remove the `useMemo` and compute the value directly so the compiler can handle memoization:

