React Compiler is enabled in this codebase and automatically memoizes derived values inside hooks. This new hook wraps `getCollectionDelta(value, previous)` in a manual `useMemo`, which is redundant when the file compiles with React Compiler — the compiler already caches this computation based on its captured `value`/`previous` dependencies. Unlike the sibling `useSidebarOrderedReports.tsx` (which documents a render-time ref cache that opts it out of the compiler), this standalone hook has no such blocker and appears compiler-friendly.

Remove the manual memoization and return the value directly, letting the compiler handle caching:

```ts
function useCollectionDelta<TValue>(value: OnyxCollection<TValue>): OnyxCollection<TValue> | undefined {
    const previous = usePrevious(value);
    return getCollectionDelta(value, previous);
